> The task is deliberately easy. Because the agent receives the estimates, an exact calculator solves it, every lost dollar comes from the agent's reasoning, its answer, or our forcing and read-out protocol, and the calculator prices a perfect tool call. The scope follows from that design: one bidder, a pay-your-bid objective, empirical win curves from eBay closing prices, and $\le$14B open checkpoints, under forced budgets up to 768 tokens and runs without forcing capped at 1{,}024 tokens and, for four models, 4{,}096. eBay itself uses proxy bidding, under which the errors we find would be harmless; we use its prices only as realistic win curves, score under the pay-your-bid rule of first-price ad exchanges, and report both rules.
